  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive education in LAC with emphasis on learners with disabilities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNESCO Santiago promotes the transformation of education systems towards more inclusive, equitable and resilient approaches that ensure quality learning opportunities for all, particularly learners with disabilities and other vulnerable groups. Through rights-based and evidence-informed policies, the Office supports countries in addressing barriers to participation, progression, completion and learning across education levels. In Latin America and the Caribbean, where 85 million people live with disabilities, UNESCO Santiago strengthens inclusive education through technical assistance, capacity development, regional cooperation and data systems such as SIRIED, helping reduce the statistical invisibility of learners with disabilities. Through RIINEE, the Office also fosters regional dialogue, peer learning and harmonized monitoring to advance inclusive education policies that leave no one behind.</narrative>
  </description>
